(KNITPASS - Deliverable D2.1) Tj T*
(Data model for digital product passports in knitwear) Tj T*
(Work package 2 - Version 1.0 - Public - 28 February 2025) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Summary) Tj T*
(This deliverable defines the data model for a digital product passport \(DPP\) for knitwear.) Tj T*
(It lists 42 data points grouped in six blocks: identity, materials, production steps,) Tj T*
(use and care, repair, and end of life. For each data point it states whether small and) Tj T*
(medium-sized knitwear makers already hold the data, and which source can provide it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Why knitwear needs its own passport profile) Tj T*
(Knitted garments are often made in small batches, with yarns bought from several spinners) Tj T*
(and dyed in separate lots. The Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation \(ESPR\)) Tj T*
(requires passports for textiles once the delegated act applies. Traceability of yarn lots) Tj T*
(is the hardest part for small producers.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
